agic shock with acute traumatic coagulopathy.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 255.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (4. Open pelvic ring disruption \(staged with orthopedic team, see companion report\).)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 235.34 cm .9 .9 .9 rg -4 -3 512 18 re f* Q q 1 0 0 1 54 235.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD (POSTOPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 218.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (1. Shattered spleen \(AAST Grade V at exploration\) with hilar injury and ~2.5 L hemoperitoneum.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 202.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (2. No hollow-viscus injury identified.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 185.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (3. Extraperitoneal pelvic hematoma, contained, non-expanding at closure.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 169.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (4. Intraperitoneal bladder-dome laceration, 2 cm, primarily repaired.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 152.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (5. As stated above, continued shock physiology requiring damage-control closure.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 132.84 cm .9 .9 .9 rg -4 -3 512 18 re f* Q q 1 0 0 1 54 132.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F2 9.5 Tf 0 2.5 TD (PROCEDURES PERFORMED)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 116.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (1. Exploratory laparotomy via midline incision.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 99.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (2. Total splenectomy for shattered spleen with hilar injury.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 83.34 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (3. Ligation of short gastric vessels; mobilization of splenic flexure.)Tj ET Q q 1 0 0 1 54 66.84 cm 0 0 0 rg BT/F1 9.5 Tf 0 3 TD (4. Primary repair of 2 cm intraperitoneal bladder-dome laceration in two layers.)Tj ET Q Q
